A||||8||Formula88||L67Formula's Class Act email||||14||
Z||000000||Formula88||12-19-2001||11:13 PM||||After some discussion in the Clutch Disengagement thread, L67Formula felt the need to email me personally to tell me what he <I>really</I> felt.  Very classy.  I'll share this with you for the enlightenment of the rest of the forum.  Why should I be the only one to benefit from his wisdom?  <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><I>Quoted private email from L67Formula to Formula88</I><BR>You want it personal so now it's personal. You're a whinyass little prick. You put out the plee for advice, info or opinion. I didn't give you information, I gave you advice. You already new about the information, I advised you to review it again. I stand by that advice and it sounds like Ed Park's procedure is what you are going to follow. Good choice. So where did I steer you wrong?<BR>     Look, I'm not a rocket scientist, or a computer analyst, or a grand wizard double blackbelt GM engineering technician parts changer. I'm just a dumbass country boy. But I read it ONCE and I GOT IT. If you didn't read it, wouldn't read it, or didn't get it, then that's YOUR problem. My cars work.(they work today, who knows about tomorrow) And talk about assinine, dropping the cradle to change the flywheel before bleeding the clutch, how cool is that?<BR>     As for not having enough time to spoon feed you, I gave you about 10 min. more than I had. I neither asked for nor expected anything in return, especially not abuse. If you can't accept it in the spirit that it's given then again that's your problem. If you have more personal comments to direct toward me you have my email address, be man enough to send it here.<BR>     My address is 3720 Cunningham Rd., Knoxville, TN 37918. If you want to drive over here and kick my ass let me know. I send you a map and I'll provide beer and sandwiches for afterwards. Sorry, no wine. Men on this side of the mountain don't drink wine.(I mean the hetero men don't)<BR>     Now, you wanna keep donin' this or get back to Formulas. This is fun but not very productive and there is a car to fix.<BR>     Wait! I just read your post again and it's really not that offensive. I'm gonna go ahead and send this because I spent so damn much time typing it. You can disregard anything above that sounds offensive. It really isn't as angry as it might sound unless you're one of those thin-skinned wine drinkers(only kidding). I stand corrected on the thinness of the flywheel issue. Again, if you're getting full rotational movement of the fork shaft and can't disengage then yes, you must shim or replace the flywheel. I agree. My concern is that you must be sure to maximize the stroke of the slave pushrod and check for adequate disengagement before committing to drop the cradle again. I honestly just did not have the time to elaborate on all this when I originally posted.<BR>     You have a good game plan, stick to it. When you get the master cylinder on the bench, if you can't bleed it then there is one problem. If you can bench bleed it then put it back on and go to the next step. One suggestion: If you pressure bleed by pumping the pedal, elevate the left rear so that the bleeder is the highest point in the system. And, if you use a vacuum bleeder you need to put teflon tape on the bleeder threads or you'll suck lots of air around the bleeder.<BR>     Your friend seems like a nice guy. Hope you get his car fixed. Again ignore anything offensive, laugh at everything else and if you still want to kick my ass the offer on the sandwiches and beer is still open. Hell, we might even find some wine if you won't let anyone see you drinking it. <BR>   jp<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not sure why he b!tches and moans in the first half and trys to be cool in the 2nd.  But, take it, and him, for what it's worth.||||reg||14
Z||000001||Cooter||12-19-2001||11:28 PM||||Pretend that I have been asleep for the past 6 months and bring me up to date on this please. I don't get it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||12-20-2001||12:04 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/016441.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/016441.html</A> <P>I started a new thread, since this didn't have anything to do with the original technical discussion.  Sorry for the confusion.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sjp777||12-20-2001||12:43 AM||||People go to email to keep that kind of crap off the forum. If you copy and paste it into a post, you're just bringing it back on. That kind of maneuver smells of edsb52<P>Reply in kind, or delete it. If you don't want to hear from him again, block his email.<P>I read the thread. Yes he was a pr*ck about it, but if you filter out the attitude the advice wasn't that bad. If you're sucking that much air it's not your flywheel. I had the same prob. I had to get 2 different new master cylinders before I got one that didn't bleed air. I tore out my hair for a week of bleeding before I realized the new master was still pulling air and got another. It happens.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg">      <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A><p>[This message has been edited by sjp777 (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||1
